        "notes": "stop_reason=finished; ## Summary I successfully fixed the cross-user ticket access vulnerability in the EventPulse API. ### Problem The API was allowing authenticated users to retrieve ticket details for tickets they didn't own, violating the security requirement that users should only be able to access their own tickets. ### Solution Added a single ownership check in `app/routes/tickets.py` in the `get_ticket` function: ```python # Users may only read their own tickets if ticket.user_id != user.id: raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"ticket not found\") ``` This check ensures that: 1. A user can only retri... [truncated, 1587 chars; full reply in trajectory.jsonl]"
